# Google Drive API Integration for Secure Document Sharing

This plan outlines the integration of Google Drive API to facilitate secure document sharing between Individual users and their respective CAs. The SaaS application acting as a mediator will not store any sensitive document data on its own servers.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This approach requires Individual users to "Connect Google Drive" and grant the `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` scope. This allows the application to create files and manage permissions for files it has created.

> [!WARNING]
> We assume the "CA" has a Google-associated email address to receive access to the shared files.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Schema (Prisma)
- Update `User` model to include:
    - `user_type`: Add `ca` to the `UserType` enum.
    - `ca_id`: A self-relation or field to link an Individual to a CA.
    - `google_refresh_token`: Encrypted string to store the user's offline access token.
    - `google_drive_folder_id`: ID of the "Compliance Docs" folder created in the user's drive.

